  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe deadline for filing the annual income tax return of an individual is on or before the fifteenth (15th) day of April of each year, covering income for the preceding taxable year.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is established under Section 51(C)(1) of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 51(C)(1) of the NIRC specifies that individuals must file their income tax returns by April 15 each year. This requirement applies to all individuals subject to income tax, ensuring that they report their income for the previous year within the stipulated timeframe.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor individual taxpayers, this means they must prepare and submit their income tax returns by April 15 to avoid penalties and interest for late filing. It is essential for taxpayers to keep accurate records of their income and deductions throughout the year to facilitate timely and accurate filing.",
